0.007475,0.011544&z=17\" target=\"_self\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Map This Location</a></p>\n<p><br></p><p>Lubbock&nbsp;<br>6202 Iola Ave Suite #900A<br>Lubbock, TX&nbsp;79424<br>(806) 783-0602 &#8211; Main line<br>(806) 783-0613 &#8211; Line 2<br>(806) 783-0615 (fax)<br><br></p><p><a href=\"http://maps.google.com/maps?q=6202+Iola+Ave+Lubbock,+TX+79424+&hl=en&sll=27.574282,-99.47427&sspn=0.007637,0.011544&z=17\" target=\"_self\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Map This Location</a></p>\n<p><br></p><p>McAllen<br>4501 West Business 83<br>STE A2<br>McAllen, TX&nbsp; 78501<br>(956) 630-2278<br>(956) 630-4806 (fax)<br><a href=\"http://maps.google.com/maps?q=4501+West+Business+83++McAllen,+TX++78501&hl=en&sll=33.53763,-101.948887&sspn=0.007181,0.011544&z=17\" target=\"_self\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Map This Location</a></p>\n<p><br></p><p>Odessa<br>4682 E. University<br>Suite 100<br>Odessa, TX&nbsp; 79762<br>(432) 550-6340<br>(432) 368-7321 (fax)<br><a href=\"http://maps.google.com/maps?q=4682+E.+University,+Odessa,+TX++79762+&hl=en&sll=26.208912,-98.269422&sspn=0.00773,0.011544&z=17\" target=\"_self\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Map This Location</a></p>\n<p><br></p><p>San Antonio<br>9514 Console<br>Suite 111<br>San Antonio, TX&nbsp; 78229<br>(210) 593-0210<br>(210) 593-0226 (fax)<br><a href=\"http://maps.google.com/maps?q=9514+Console,+San+Antonio,+TX++78229+&hl=en&sll=31.880191,-102.325308&sspn=0.007316,0.011544&z=17\" target=\"_self\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Map This Location</a></p>\n<p><br></p><p>Tyler<br>3800 Paluxy Drive<br>Suite 330<br>Tyler, TX&nbsp; 75703<br>(903) 509-9008<br>(903) 509-9309 (fax)<br><a href=\"http://maps.google.com/maps?q=3800+Paluxy+Drive,+Tyler,+TX++79762&hl=en&z=17\" target=\"_self\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Map This Location</a></p>\n<p><br></p><p>Victoria<br>2306 Leary Lane,<br><span style=\"color: var( --e-global-color-text ); font-family: var( --e-global-typography-text-font-family ), Archivo; font-weight: var( --e-global-typography-text-font-weight ); font-size: 1rem;\">Suite&nbsp;400 </span><span style=\"color: var( --e-global-color-text ); font-family: var( --e-global-typography-text-font-family ), Archivo; font-weight: var( --e-global-typography-text-font-weight ); font-size: 1rem;\">Victoria, TX&nbsp; 77901</span><br></p><p>(361) 573-4185<br>(361) 573-1290 (fax)<br><a href=\"https://maps.google.com/maps?q=2306+Leary+Lane,+Victoria,+TX++77901&hl=en\" target=\"_self\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Map This Location</a></p>\n<h2><br></h2><h2>Tax Information</h2>\n<p><br></p><p>Texas Lottery Federal, and state tax withholdings on winnings for U.S. citizens or residents.&nbsp;</p>\n<p><br></p>\n<table id=\"tablepress-USResidentsTax-no-3\" class=\"tablepress tablepress-id-USResidentsTax tablepress-responsive\">\n<thead>\n<tr class=\"row-1\">\n\t<th class=\"column-1\">Winnings</th><th class=\"column-2\">Tax Category</th><th class=\"column-3\">Percentage</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody class=\"row-striping row-hover\">\n<tr class=\"row-2\">\n\t<td class=\"column-1\">Over $5,000</td><td class=\"column-2\">State Tax</td><td class=\"column-3\">0.0%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-3\">\n\t<td class=\"column-1\">Over $5,000</td><td class=\"column-2\">Federal Tax</td><td class=\"column-3\">24.0%</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n<p><br></p><p>If the winner is not a U.S. citizen or is not a US resident, Texas Lottery tax withholdings on winnings are as such:</p>\n<p><br></p>\n<table id=\"tablepress-NonUSTax-no-3\" class=\"tablepress tablepress-id-NonUSTax tablepress-responsive\">\n<thead>\n<tr class=\"row-1\">\n\t<th class=\"column-1\">Winnings</th><th class=\"column-2\">Tax Category</th><th class=\"column-3\">Percentage</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody class=\"row-striping row-hover\">\n<tr class=\"row-2\">\n\t<td class=\"column-1\">Over $600 or more</td><td class=\"column-2\">State Tax</td><td class=\"column-3\">0.0%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-3\">\n\t<td class=\"column-1\">Over $600 or more</td><td class=\"column-2\">Federal Tax</td><td class=\"column-3\">30.0%</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n<figure><br></figure><figure><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"/wp-media/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/texas.jpg\" sizes=\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\" srcset=\"/wp-media/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/texas.jpg 894w, /wp-media/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/texas-300x143.jpg 300w, /wp-media/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/texas-768x367.jpg 768w\" alt=\"Texas Lottery\" width=\"800\" height=\"382\"><p></p>\n<figcaption></figcaption>\n</figure>\n<h2><br></h2><h2>About the Texas Lottery</h2>\n<p>The lottery in Texas was launched in 1992 and has since established itself as one of the most successful state lotteries. It’s awarded over $43 billion in prizes, with the top winner thus far claiming $227 million in 2019.&nbsp;Its first offering was Lone Star Millions, a scratch game that resulted in over 20 million tickets sold on the first day, setting a world record. There are now 17 draws in eight different games: Pick 3, Daily 4, All or Nothing, Cash Five, Lotto Texas, Texas Two-Step, Powerball, and Mega Millions.</p>\n<p></p>\n<p>The Texas Lottery allocates a significant portion of its revenue to fund various sectors. Overall, it’s contributed around $25 billion to education and more than $130 million to <a href=\"https://www.texvet.org/\">Texas veterans</a>. When Texas residents play the lottery, they’re increasing their chances of winning the jackpot, but they’re also improving others’ lives.</p>\n<h2>&nbsp;</h2>\n<h2>Texas Lottery FAQ</h2><div><br></div>\n<p></p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t</section>\n\t\t\t\t<section class=\"has_eae_slider elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-50cb398 elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default\" data-eae-slider=\"14021\" data-id=\"50cb398\" data-element_type=\"section\" data-e-type=\"section\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"has_eae_slider elementor-column elementor-col-100 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-4e4035d\" data-eae-slider=\"99462\" data-id=\"4e4035d\" data-element_type=\"column\" data-e-type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-d769569 elementor-widget elementor-widget-eael-adv-accordion\" data-id=\"d769569\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"eael-adv-accordion.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t            <div class=\"eael-adv-accordion\" id=\"eael-adv-accordion-d769569\" data-scroll-on-click=\"no\" data-scroll-speed=\"300\" data-accordion-id=\"d769569\" data-accordion-type=\"accordion\" data-toogle-speed=\"300\">\n            <div class=\"eael-accordion-list\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"how-do-you-purchase-lottery-tickets-in-texas\" class=\"elementor-tab-title eael-accordion-header\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tab=\"1\" aria-controls=\"elementor-tab-content-2251\"><span class=\"eael-advanced-accordion-icon-closed\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-accordion-icon fas fa-plus\"></i></span><span class=\"eael-advanced-accordion-icon-opened\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-accordion-icon fas fa-minus\"></i></span><span class=\"eael-accordion-tab-title\">How do you purchase lottery tickets in Texas?</span><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-toggle fas fa-angle-right\"></i></div><div id=\"elementor-tab-content-2251\" class=\"eael-accordion-content clearfix\" data-tab=\"1\" aria-labelledby=\"how-do-you-purchase-lottery-tickets-in-texas\"><p>If you’re over the age of 18, you can buy lottery tickets at licensed retailers. This is the only legal option in Texas since online purchases and sales by phone and mail aren’t allowed.</p><p> </p><p>Additionally, you can buy tickets in advance for every lottery game. Cash Five allows up to 12 advanced draws, while Lotto Texas, Texas Two Step, Powerball, and Mega Millions offer ten advanced draws. You can purchase a maximum of 24 advanced draws for the remaining lottery games.</p></div>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div><div class=\"eael-accordion-list\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"what-lottery-games-can-you-play-in-texas\" class=\"elementor-tab-title eael-accordion-header\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tab=\"2\" aria-controls=\"elementor-tab-content-2252\"><span class=\"eael-advanced-accordion-icon-closed\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-accordion-icon fas fa-plus\"></i></span><span class=\"eael-advanced-accordion-icon-opened\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-accordion-icon fas fa-minus\"></i></span><span class=\"eael-accordion-tab-title\">What lottery games can you play in Texas?</span><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-toggle fas fa-angle-right\"></i></div><div id=\"elementor-tab-content-2252\" class=\"eael-accordion-content clearfix\" data-tab=\"2\" aria-labelledby=\"what-lottery-games-can-you-play-in-texas\"><p>There are various lottery games you can play in Texas. Furthermore, many of these games occur several times a day, which means you have multiple chances of winning. In total, there are 17 different draws in eight different games, each with their own Texas Lottery numbers:</p><p> </p><p>Pick 3 Morning, Day, Evening, Night &#8211; Choose three numbers between 0-9</p><p>Daily 4 Morning, Day, Evening, Night &#8211; Choose four numbers between 0-9</p><p>All or Nothing Morning, Day, Evening, Night &#8211; Choose 12 numbers between 1-24</p><p>Cash Five &#8211; Choose five numbers between 1-35</p><p>Lotto Texas &#8211; Choose six numbers between 1-54</p><p>Texas Two Step &#8211; Choose four numbers between 1-35 along with an additional number</p><p>Texas Lottery Powerball &#8211; Choose five numbers between 1-69 and another number between 1-26</p><p>Texas Lottery Mega Millions &#8211; Choose five numbers between 1-70 and an extra number between 1-25</p><p>All games offer a top prize, while Lotto Texas, Texas Two Step, Powerball, and Mega Millions have a jackpot up for grabs. Furthermore, take note that you can’t play the Texas Lottery Lucky for Life game.</p></div>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div><div class=\"eael-accordion-list\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"where-and-how-do-you-claim-winnings-from-the-texas-lottery\" class=\"elementor-tab-title eael-accordion-header\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tab=\"3\" aria-controls=\"elementor-tab-content-2253\"><span class=\"eael-advanced-accordion-icon-closed\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-accordion-icon fas fa-plus\"></i></span><span class=\"eael-advanced-accordion-icon-opened\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-accordion-icon fas fa-minus\"></i></span><span class=\"eael-accordion-tab-title\">Where and how do you claim winnings from the Texas Lottery?</span><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-toggle fas fa-angle-right\"></i></div><div id=\"elementor-tab-content-2253\" class=\"eael-accordion-content clearfix\" data-tab=\"3\" aria-labelledby=\"where-and-how-do-you-claim-winnings-from-the-texas-lottery\"><p>If you win a prize worth $599 or less, you can claim it at your local retailer or visit one of the Texas Lottery Claim Centers. Additionally, you can choose to post your signed ticket via registered mail to the Texas State Lottery.</p><p> </p><p>Prizes worth $600 or more can be claimed at any of the Texas Lottery Claim Centers. Alternatively, you can complete a claim form and mail it to the Texas Lottery. Remember to sign the back of your ticket and post it as well.</p><p> </p><p>You can claim any prize over $2.5 million at the Texas Lottery Commission in Austin. You’ll need to make an appointment and visit the center in person.</p><p> </p><p>If you submit your claim via post, you can expect to wait between four to six weeks to receive your winnings. Additionally, you must claim any winning tickets within 180 days.</p></div>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div><div class=\"eael-accordion-list\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"how-do-you-play-and-win-in-the-texas-lottery\" class=\"elementor-tab-title eael-accordion-header\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tab=\"4\" aria-controls=\"elementor-tab-content-2254\"><span class=\"eael-advanced-accordion-icon-closed\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-accordion-icon fas fa-plus\"></i></span><span class=\"eael-advanced-accordion-icon-opened\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-accordion-icon fas fa-minus\"></i></span><span class=\"eael-accordion-tab-title\">How do you play and win in the Texas Lottery?</span><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-toggle fas fa-angle-right\"></i></div><div id=\"elementor-tab-content-2254\" class=\"eael-accordion-content clearfix\" data-tab=\"4\" aria-labelledby=\"how-do-you-play-and-win-in-the-texas-lottery\"><p>To win in the Texas Lottery, you need to select the same numbers picked in the draw. For instance, Lotto Texas incorporates numbers 1-54, and its rules state that you must choose six numbers within this range.</p><p> </p><p>If you correctly predict all six of the Texas Lottery winning numbers, you’ll win the grand jackpot. However, you can still win some cash if you manage to match a minimum of two numbers.</p></div>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div><div class=\"eael-accordion-list\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"whats-the-biggest-texas-lottery-win\" class=\"elementor-tab-title eael-accordion-header\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tab=\"5\" aria-controls=\"elementor-tab-content-2255\"><span class=\"eael-advanced-accordion-icon-closed\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-accordion-icon fas fa-plus\"></i></span><span class=\"eael-advanced-accordion-icon-opened\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-accordion-icon fas fa-minus\"></i></span><span class=\"eael-accordion-tab-title\">What’s the biggest Texas Lottery win?</span><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-toggle fas fa-angle-right\"></i></div><div id=\"elementor-tab-content-2255\" class=\"eael-accordion-content clearfix\" data-tab=\"5\" aria-labelledby=\"whats-the-biggest-texas-lottery-win\"><p>Although there have been many Texas Lottery winners, the largest payout occurred in October 2019, when a Leander resident won $227 million in the Mega Millions jackpot. The winner went with the cash option and received $157,091,592 in a single lump sum.</p></div>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div><div class=\"eael-accordion-list\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"when-is-the-texas-lottery-results-draw\" class=\"elementor-tab-title eael-accordion-header\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tab=\"6\" aria-controls=\"elementor-tab-content-2256\"><span class=\"eael-advanced-accordion-icon-closed\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-accordion-icon fas fa-plus\"></i></span><span class=\"eael-advanced-accordion-icon-opened\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-accordion-icon fas fa-minus\"></i></span><span class=\"eael-accordion-tab-title\">When is the Texas Lottery results draw?</span><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-toggle fas fa-angle-right\"></i></div><div id=\"elementor-tab-content-2256\" class=\"eael-accordion-content clearfix\" data-tab=\"6\" aria-labelledby=\"when-is-the-texas-lottery-results-draw\"><p>The results of the Texas Lottery games take place as follows:</p><p> </p><p>Pick 3 Morning, Daily 4 Morning, All or Nothing Morning draws take place Monday to Saturday at 10:00 am</p><p>Pick 3 Day, Daily 4 Day, All or Nothing Day draws take place Monday to Saturday at 12:27 pm</p><p>Pick 3 Evening, Daily 4 Evening, All or Nothing Evening draws take place Monday to Saturday at 6:00 pm</p><p>Pick 3 Night, Daily 4 Night, and All or Nothing Night draws take place Monday to Saturday at 10:12 pm</p><p>Cash Five draws take place Monday to Saturday at 10:12 pm</p><p>Lotto Texas draws take place Wednesday and Saturday at 10:12 pm</p><p>Texas Two Step draws take place Monday and Thursday at 10:12 pm</p><p>Powerball draws take place Wednesday and Saturday at 10:12 pm</p><p>Mega Millions draws take place Tuesday and Friday at 10:12 pm</p></div>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div><div class=\"eael-accordion-list\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"what-is-the-texas-lottery-second-chance\" class=\"elementor-tab-title eael-accordion-header\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tab=\"7\" aria-controls=\"elementor-tab-content-2257\"><span class=\"eael-advanced-accordion-icon-closed\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-accordion-icon fas fa-plus\"></i></span><span class=\"eael-advanced-accordion-icon-opened\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-accordion-icon fas fa-minus\"></i></span><span class=\"eael-accordion-tab-title\">What is the Texas Lottery second chance?</span><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-toggle fas fa-angle-right\"></i></div><div id=\"elementor-tab-content-2257\" class=\"eael-accordion-content clearfix\" data-tab=\"7\" aria-labelledby=\"what-is-the-texas-lottery-second-chance\"><p>You can download the Texas Lottery app and get access to a variety of features. These include more winning opportunities, viewing results, locating authorized retailers, and finding your favorite Texas Lottery scratch tickets, to name a few.</p><p> </p><p>Additionally, you can access Texas Lottery codes and enter second-chance drawings on non-winning picks by using the Texas Lottery ticket scanner within the app.</p></div>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div><div class=\"eael-accordion-list\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"do-i-have-to-pay-tax-on-texas-lottery-winnings\" class=\"elementor-tab-title eael-accordion-header\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tab=\"8\" aria-controls=\"elementor-tab-content-2258\"><span class=\"eael-advanced-accordion-icon-closed\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-accordion-icon fas fa-plus\"></i></span><span class=\"eael-advanced-accordion-icon-opened\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-accordion-icon fas fa-minus\"></i></span><span class=\"eael-accordion-tab-title\">Do I have to pay tax on Texas Lottery winnings?</span><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-toggle fas fa-angle-right\"></i></div><div id=\"elementor-tab-content-2258\" class=\"eael-accordion-content clearfix\" data-tab=\"8\" aria-labelledby=\"do-i-have-to-pay-tax-on-texas-lottery-winnings\"><p>Yes. If you’re a US citizen or a Texas resident, any prize over $5,000 attracts the following taxes:</p><p> </p><p>State tax: 0%</p><p> </p><p>Federal tax: 24%</p><p> </p><p>Total: 24%</p></div>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div></div>\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t</section>\n\t\t\t\t<section class=\"has_eae_slider elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-cb5f7ba elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default\" data-eae-slider=\"63406\" data-id=\"cb5f7ba\" data-element_type=\"section\" data-e-type=\"section\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"has_eae_slider elementor-column elementor-col-50 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-9d2c203\" data-eae-slider=\"81070\" data-id=\"9d2c203\" data-element_type=\"column\" data-e-type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-4b70335 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"4b70335\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>Got more questions about the Texas Lottery?</p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"has_eae_slider elementor-column elementor-col-50 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-9af4c19\" data-eae-slider=\"21409\" data-id=\"9af4c19\" data-element_type=\"column\" data-e-type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-176714f elementor-button-success elementor-align-center elementor-widget elementor-widget-button\" data-id=\"176714f\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"button.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-button-wrapper\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"elementor-button elementor-button-link elementor-size-lg\" href=\"/Contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<span class=\"elementor-button-content-wrapper\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span class=\"elementor-button-text\">Send Us an Email</span>\n\t\t\t\t\t</span>\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t</section>\n\t\t\t\t<section class=\"has_eae_slider elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-180dc5e elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default\" data-eae-slider=\"97040\" data-id=\"180dc5e\" data-element_type=\"section\" data-e-type=\"section\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"has_eae_slider elementor-column elementor-col-100 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-2aad32e\" data-eae-slider=\"87031\" data-id=\"2aad32e\" data-element_type=\"column\" data-e-type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-7e00784 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\" data-id=\"7e00784\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"html.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"How do you purchase lottery tickets in Texas?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"If you\\u2019re over the age of 18, you can buy lottery tickets at licensed retailers. This is the only legal option in Texas since online purchases and sales by phone and mail aren\\u2019t allowed.\\n\\n \\n\\nAdditionally, you can buy tickets in advance for every lottery game. Cash Five allows up to 12 advanced draws, while Lotto Texas, Texas Two Step, Powerball, and Mega Millions offer ten advanced draws. You can purchase a maximum of 24 advanced draws for the remaining lottery games.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What lottery games can you play in Texas?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"There are various lottery games you can play in Texas. Furthermore, many of these games occur several times a day, which means you have multiple chances of winning. In total, there are 17 different draws in eight different games, each with their own Texas Lottery numbers:\\n\\n \\n\\nPick 3 Morning, Day, Evening, Night - Choose three numbers between 0-9\\n\\nDaily 4 Morning, Day, Evening, Night - Choose four numbers between 0-9\\n\\nAll or Nothing Morning, Day, Evening, Night - Choose 12 numbers between 1-24\\n\\nCash Five - Choose five numbers between 1-35\\n\\nLotto Texas - Choose six numbers between 1-54\\n\\nTexas Two Step - Choose four numbers between 1-35 along with an additional number\\n\\nTexas Lottery Powerball - Choose five numbers between 1-69 and another number between 1-26\\n\\nTexas Lottery Mega Millions - Choose five numbers between 1-70 and an extra number between 1-25\\n\\nAll games offer a top prize, while Lotto Texas, Texas Two Step, Powerball, and Mega Millions have a jackpot up for grabs. Furthermore, take note that you can\\u2019t play the Texas Lottery Lucky for Life game.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Where and how do you claim winnings from the Texas Lottery?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"If you win a prize worth $599 or less, you can claim it at your local retailer or visit one of the Texas Lottery Claim Centers. Additionally, you can choose to post your signed ticket via registered mail to the Texas State Lottery.\\n\\n \\n\\nPrizes worth $600 or more can be claimed at any of the Texas Lottery Claim Centers. Alternatively, you can complete a claim form and mail it to the Texas Lottery. Remember to sign the back of your ticket and post it as well.\\n\\n \\n\\nYou can claim any prize over $2.5 million at the Texas Lottery Commission in Austin. You\\u2019ll need to make an appointment and visit the center in person.\\n\\n \\n\\nIf you submit your claim via post, you can expect to wait between four to six weeks to receive your winnings. Additionally, you must claim any winning tickets within 180 days.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"How do you play and win in the Texas Lottery?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"To win in the Texas Lottery, you need to select the same numbers picked in the draw. For instance, Lotto Texas incorporates numbers 1-54, and its rules state that you must choose six numbers within this range.\\n\\n \\n\\nIf you correctly predict all six of the Texas Lottery winning numbers, you\\u2019ll win the grand jackpot. However, you can still win some cash if you manage to match a minimum of two numbers.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What\\u2019s the biggest Texas Lottery win?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Although there have been many Texas Lottery winners, the largest payout occurred in October 2019, when a Leander resident won $227 million in the Mega Millions jackpot. The winner went with the cash option and received $157,091,592 in a single lump sum.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"When is the Texas Lottery results draw?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"The results of the Texas Lottery games take place as follows:\\n\\n \\n\\nPick 3 Morning, Daily 4 Morning, All or Nothing Morning draws take place Monday to Saturday at 10:00 am\\n\\nPick 3 Day, Daily 4 Day, All or Nothing Day draws take place Monday to Saturday at 12:27 pm\\n\\nPick 3 Evening, Daily 4 Evening, All or Nothing Evening draws take place Monday to Saturday at 6:00 pm\\n\\nPick 3 Night, Daily 4 Night, and All or Nothing Night draws take place Monday to Saturday at 10:12 pm\\n\\nCash Five draws take place Monday to Saturday at 10:12 pm\\n\\nLotto Texas draws take place Wednesday and Saturday at 10:12 pm\\n\\nTexas Two Step draws take place Monday and Thursday at 10:12 pm\\n\\nPowerball draws take place Wednesday and Saturday at 10:12 pm\\n\\nMega Millions draws take place Tuesday and Friday at 10:12 pm\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What is the Texas Lottery second chance?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"You can download the Texas Lottery app and get access to a variety of features. These include more winning opportunities, viewing results, locating authorized retailers, and finding your favorite Texas Lottery scratch tickets, to name a few.\\n\\n \\n\\nAdditionally, you can access Texas Lottery codes and enter second-chance drawings on non-winning picks by using the Texas Lottery ticket scanner within the app.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Do I have to pay tax on Texas Lottery winnings?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Yes. If you\\u2019re a US citizen or a Texas resident, any prize over $5,000 attracts the following taxes:\\n\\n \\n\\nState tax: 0%\\n\\n \\n\\nFederal tax: 24%\\n\\n \\n\\nTotal: 24%\"}}]}</script>\r\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t</section>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t",
